    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Nellie sits beside the Walhonding River, a winding waterway that has shaped the village’s early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nellie%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Just north‑west of the village stands the 1930s‑era Mohawk Dam, a dry flood‑control structure that once protected local farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nellie%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village traces its roots to 1757, when pioneers William Darling and Sofia Sadowski settled the area that would become Nellie.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wvhistoricalsociety.org/ct-menu-item-3/ct-menu-item-13"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nellie lies in central‑eastern Ohio, northwest of Coshocton and close enough to Newark and Zanesville for easy day trips.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.citydirectory.us/village-nellie.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Walhonding Valley Historical Society keeps Nellie’s story alive with a museum, newsletters, and annual meetings that honor local heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
